  "details": "On oculus, meta has stated that users under the age of 13 aren't allowed on the platform. However, children have not followed these rules, and think they can stomp all over other players. They also discover avatars that aren't for kids, to say the least. If your not gonna ban them, the best alternative is to make a junior account system, similar to rec room. Kids would not be allowed to get NSFW avatars, be outright muted unless the player unmutes them, and their avatar is automatically hidden. This would be a great addition, as not only does it eliminate the threat of children, but also keeps them safe. Another optional addition to this, on the junior players end, everyone else is muted to them. Extra protection, as well as some peace to everyone over the age of 13. Thank you for your time, and please consider this.",
